<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila hydei 2.3 µm Turing wavenumber (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 of the 2.344 µm (2.344e-06 m, log10=-5.630) Schnakenberg-Turing patch for Drosophila hydei at geological age 0 Ma. Dispersion goodness-of-fit including the oscillatory mode: Pearson r=0.9985, RMSE=0.0187, KS=0.125. Equal-diffusion σ_max=-0.1025. γ-sweep wavelengths 4.688, 2.344, 1.172, 0.781 µm, and the γ=4 FFT ratio is 0.5. Specimen foreground 0.5504 versus simulation occupancy 0.5, circularity 0.0615 versus 0.785, coherency 0.679 versus 0.25. GIF CV similarity 96.0 on 12 frames at 720×540. Predecessor D. heteroneura 175.4 µm (ratio 74.83), primordium slot exactly 50×, successor D. kikkawai 93.41 µm. Weighted score 87.5/100. Overall 87.5/100 (faithfulness 86.9, reproducibility 88.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a4df1e95; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0.py at a4df1e95, image/png, 338902 B, 1474×924 px, artifact_sha256 7573be404d095e4c00b949b01f9fa1d701d909bbdd0d3059c15f21aeed44aa88 (sha256 7573be404d095e4c00b949b01f9fa1d701d909bbdd0d3059c15f21aeed44aa88), spec_fingerprint 2f7c144dc5fc54295dbbe4b347ff7ae9a8e0dde0cfac395b2f56b886e1932c0d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2f7c144dc5fc54295dbbe4b347ff7ae9a8e0dde0cfac395b2f56b886e1932c0d; artifact_sha256: 7573be404d095e4c00b949b01f9fa1d701d909bbdd0d3059c15f21aeed44aa88; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=258a7865f6ffc435..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=638a3272e18240dc..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=483d25650491bb68..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4266c3fd37318a28..., datasets/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=c32568bb24399205...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used here. | Pitnick, Spicer and Markow 1995: giant Drosophila sperm; the PNAS abstract says some species exceed ten male body lengths. | Gompel et al. 2005: a Drosophila pigment spot with a cis-regulatory origin.; reconstructed_in_script: Length unit chosen so λ_c(γ=1)=2.344 µm, with λ scaling as γ^(-1/2). | Chronoseries ratios against 175.4 µm, 117.2 µm and 93.41 µm at geological age 0 Ma. | Hilbert-envelope estimate of Re(σ) on the oscillatory Fourier mode.; transfer_boundary: The cohort law is applied at the assigned detail scale. It is not a parameter estimate from a hydei cuticle micrograph.; does_not_claim: That a 2.3 µm Turing instability has been measured in D. hydei. | That the whole-animal photograph resolves that wavelength. | That the campaign epithet of a 58 mm sperm was re-measured in this loop. | That cis-regulatory pigment control is absent. | A signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Residual, not a pass-1 item: no independent second assessor scored this script.",
        "remediation needed: Residual, not a pass-1 item: the specimen is a whole-animal photograph and does not resolve 2.3 µm.",
        "remediation needed: Residual, not a pass-1 item: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent, so the nanopubs are unsigned." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.75e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila hydei 2.3 µm Turing wavenumber (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "λ(γ) = 2.344/sqrt(γ) µm is monotonic on {0.25, 1, 4, 9} and the γ=4 PDE returns FFT wavelength 1.172 µm (ratio 0.5, reference null 0.25). Setting D_u=D_v removes the Turing band (σ_max=-0.1025). a and b stay at the Schnakenberg values that give det=1." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

