<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila hydei 2.3 µm Turing wavenumber (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Drosophila hydei)",
        "Drosophila hydei 2.3 µm Turing wavenumber (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila hydei morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila hydei specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila hydei" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.",
        "does_not_claim: That a 2.3 µm Turing instability has been measured in D. hydei.",
        "does_not_claim: That cis-regulatory pigment control is absent.",
        "does_not_claim: That the campaign epithet of a 58 mm sperm was re-measured in this loop.",
        "does_not_claim: That the whole-animal photograph resolves that wavelength.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronoseries ratios against 175.4 µm, 117.2 µm and 93.41 µm at geological age 0 Ma.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Hilbert-envelope estimate of Re(σ) on the oscillatory Fourier mode.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Length unit chosen so λ_c(γ=1)=2.344 µm, with λ scaling as γ^(-1/2).",
        "reported_in_source: Gompel et al. 2005: a Drosophila pigment spot with a cis-regulatory origin.",
        "reported_in_source: Pitnick, Spicer and Markow 1995: giant Drosophila sperm; the PNAS abstract says some species exceed ten male body lengths.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: The cohort law is applied at the assigned detail scale. It is not a parameter estimate from a hydei cuticle micrograph." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila hydei (Giant-Sperm Repleta Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-hydei-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_hydei_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila hydei; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used here. | Pitnick, Spicer and Markow 1995: giant Drosophila sperm; the PNAS abstract says some species exceed ten male body lengths. | Gompel et al. 2005: a Drosophila pigment spot with a cis-regulatory origin.; reconstructed_in_script: Length unit chosen so λ_c(γ=1)=2.344 µm, with λ scaling as γ^(-1/2). | Chronoseries ratios against 175.4 µm, 117.2 µm and 93.41 µm at geological age 0 Ma. | Hilbert-envelope estimate of Re(σ) on the oscillatory Fourier mode.; transfer_boundary: The cohort law is applied at the assigned detail scale. It is not a parameter estimate from a hydei cuticle micrograph.; does_not_claim: That a 2.3 µm Turing instability has been measured in D. hydei. | That the whole-animal photograph resolves that wavelength. | That the campaign epithet of a 58 mm sperm was re-measured in this loop. | That cis-regulatory pigment control is absent. | A signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
